/Title (Psychological barriers such as decision fatigue and perceived future value further delay action. As Glawson \(2021\) notes, consumer culture normalises continuous acquisition, reinforcing inaction. Consequently, clutter reflects a broader failure of circular systems, contributing to household strain and environmental impacts, including textile waste overflow in regions such as Ghana \(Quashie-Idun, 2025\).)
